    <string name="about_source_lunar">Lunar calendar and solar terms: computed on the phone with lunar-java (MIT).</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Dayloom has no server of its own and collects nothing: no analytics, no crash reports, no ads.\n\nYour settings, places and keys stay on this phone. There is no cloud backup; moving to a new phone copies your settings but not your keys, which are encrypted with this phone\'s Android Keystore.\n\nThe app only contacts the services of the modules you turn on, and sends each only what it needs: the coordinates of Home to MET Norway, your stops to Entur, what you type into place search to Google or Open-Meteo, your saved places to Google Routes, your team to football-data.org, and your token to your own Miniflux server. An article\'s text goes to your AI endpoint only when you tap Summarize.\n\nThe app asks for no location permission. It asks for the notification permission only when you turn on a notification.</string>
